<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτολμ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>submit</i> or <i>endure</i> to do, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ ἐπιτολμάτω κραδίη καὶ θυμὸς
					ἀκούειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.353
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				445
			</span></i> : abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπετόλμησε</span> he
				<i>stood firm,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.238
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>dare, venture,</i> abs., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.594
			</span></i> : c. inf., ib.<i><span class="en">
				671
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.710
			</span></i> : c. dat., <i>venture upon,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ διαβάσει, ἔργῳ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phil.</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				69
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ δίφρῳ</span>
			<i>mount</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
					<u>Ren.Ves.</u>
					2.36
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				7.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> ap. Suid.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστάθμητον.</span>
			</div>
